Round 18 (2026-02-27)

What landed
- Files changed:
  - `clang/aot/emit.c`
- AOT counting policy change in emitter:
  - `aot_emit_counting(cfg)` now enables emitted `aot_itrs_inc()` only for `-s`/`-D` (`stats || step_by_step`).
  - `-S` no longer forces counting in generated AOT code.
- Added `LAM_ERA_MASK` fast paths in emitted APP-LAM flows:
  - Head LAM (`head=1`): if lambda binder is erased, generated code skips reading/capturing APP arg and installs erased env cell (`term_sub_set(term_new_era(),1)`).
  - Expression APP with `fun_tag == LAM`: same erased-binder behavior (skip arg ALO capture, keep env-depth shape).

Why
- Benchmarks are executed with `-S`; counting in compiled hot paths was avoidable overhead.
- APP-LAM over erased binders should not capture args; previous emitted code still did, creating unnecessary residualization/work.

